Extract what each mathematical statement introduces and uses.

Return JSON only — no markdown, no explanation. A JSON array with one entry per input statement. Each entry MUST echo the input statement's `id` verbatim — that is how we pair your answer back to the right statement:
[
  {"id": "<copy id from the input>", "defines": [{"description": "...", "pattern": "..."}], "uses": ["...", ...]},
  ...
]

"defines": notation explicitly introduced in that statement (paper-specific symbols/objects/concepts, custom operators, named shorthands). Look for "Let X be", "Denote by", "We write X for", "Define X", etc. Each "pattern" is a regex; use \\\\ for LaTeX backslash. Skip standard math (\\mathbb{R}, \\sum, \\int, \\leq, etc.) and generic variable letters. The "description" should briefly explain what the notation means or how it is defined.

"uses": exact substrings of notation used but not introduced in that statement. For isolated symbols include delimiters ("$G$" not "G"). Skip standard math and anything in that statement's "defines". Never include \\ref, \\cite, \\label, \\eqref or similar.

Example input:
[
  {"id": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111", "kind": "Definition", "body": "Let $G$ be a locally compact group. Denote by $\\mu_G$ its left Haar measure. A function $f$ is $\\mu_G$-integrable if $\\int_G |f|\\,d\\mu_G < \\infty$."},
  {"id": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222", "kind": "Theorem", "body": "Every $\\mu_G$-integrable $f$ on $G$ satisfies $\\|\\hat{f}\\|_\\infty \\leq \\|\\mu_G\\|$ (see \\cite{folland})."}
]

Example output:
[
  {"id": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111", "defines": [{"description": "left Haar measure of G", "pattern": "\\\\mu_G"}, {"description": "mu_G-integrable function", "pattern": "\\\\mu_G-integrable"}], "uses": []},
  {"id": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222", "defines": [], "uses": ["\\mu_G-integrable", "\\mu_G", "$G$", "\\hat{f}"]}
]

Statements:
[
{% for s in statements %}
  {"id": "{{ s.statement_id }}", "kind": "{{ s.kind | title }}"{% if s.note %}, "note": {{ s.note | tojson }}{% endif %}, "body": {{ s.body | tojson }}}{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
]
